00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.310
The first thing we're going to do with
the sticks is create what's called an

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:32.530
airfoil and this allows the stick to get
a lift because the air is flying faster

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:36.540
on top and lower on bottom not going to
go into too much detail but that's

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:41.400
basically what it's going to do. Now this
is a side view of the stick. To do this

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:46.599
we're basically going to make a line on
the stick vertically two to three

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:51.520
millimeters from the edge--from here in.
So let's go ahead and do that as you'll

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.780
see each of these individual marks right
here are one millimeter so it's a very

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:59.290
small increment so we're gonna go up to
the third one right here on each of the

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:03.780
sticks and we're going to make three
marks just like this: There's one mark

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:08.590
Two marks... and Three marks. Once we have the three marks then we could take the

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:12.780
ruler and place it directly next to the
marks not on top of it because you need

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.380
room for the pencil. Hold it steady
and then draw a line going all the way

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.720
down through those three marks now
you'll have something that looks like

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:24.520
this and you're ready to take off the
excess wood. Now we're going to remove

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:30.220
the excess wood along that line that we
took on this edge so that it looks

